* Task 4 fixture: Host-variable references in native SQL clauses
* Demonstrates FR-21 requirement: native SQL host vars bind to DEFINE DATA declarations
* Tests both bare (#-prefixed) and colon-prefixed forms, including reserved-word case (:DATE)
*
* Expected host-var refs (normalized: sigil kept, colon stripped, upper-cased):
*   - #NAME from INTO (bare form)
*   - #SALARY from INTO (bare form)
*   - #PERS-ID from WHERE (bare form)
*   - DATE from WHERE (colon-prefixed reserved word, :DATE)
* Zero false edges: column names (COL1, COL2) and table name (SQL-PERSONNEL) NOT refs

DEFINE DATA LOCAL
  1 #NAME (A30)
  1 #SALARY (N9.2)
  1 #PERS-ID (N5)
  1 #DATE (D)
END-DEFINE

SELECT COL1, COL2 INTO #NAME, #SALARY FROM SQL-PERSONNEL WHERE DEPT = #PERS-ID AND START_DATE >= :DATE
  CALLNAT 'PROCESS'
END-SELECT

END
